@startuml 08-webhook-race-condition
!theme plain
title Webhook Race Condition Analysis

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Customer as C
participant "Browser" as B
participant "Stripe API" as Stripe #FFE0B2
participant "Stripe Webhook" as WH #FFE0B2
participant "User Return Flow" as RF
participant "Contract" as Contract #E1F5FE
participant "Order::finalizeOrder()" as FO
database "oxorder" as DB

== Scenario 1: User Returns BEFORE Webhook ==

note over C, DB #E8F5E9
    **HAPPY PATH** (Current Implementation)
    User returns first, webhook is just confirmation
end note

C -> Stripe: Complete payment
Stripe --> B: Redirect to success_url
B -> RF: checkoutSuccess()

RF -> Contract: Load by ID
Contract --> RF: Contract (PENDING)

RF -> Contract: fulfillCondition('payment_authorized')
RF -> Contract: Transition to READY_TO_COMMIT
RF -> FO: finalizeOrder()
FO -> DB: INSERT oxorder
FO --> RF: ORDER_STATE_OK

RF -> Contract: commitToOrder(orderId)
RF -> Contract: Transition to COMMITTED

note right of Contract
    Contract state: COMMITTED
    Order exists: YES
end note

... later ...

Stripe -> WH: payment_intent.succeeded
WH -> Contract: Find by provider_order_id
WH -> WH: Contract is COMMITTED
WH -> WH: Order already exists
WH --> Stripe: 200 OK (no action needed)

== Scenario 2: Webhook Arrives BEFORE User Returns ==

note over C, DB #FFCDD2
    **RACE CONDITION**
    Webhook tries to fulfill before user returns
end note

C -> Stripe: Complete payment

group Webhook arrives first
    Stripe -> WH: payment_intent.succeeded
    WH -> Contract: Find by provider_order_id
    Contract --> WH: Contract (PENDING)

    note right of WH #FFCDD2
        **PROBLEM:**
        Contract is still PENDING
        No order exists yet
        What should webhook do?
    end note

    alt Option A: Webhook Creates Order (Risky)
        WH -> WH: fulfillCondition()
        WH -> WH: Transition to READY_TO_COMMIT
        WH -> FO: finalizeOrder()

        note right of FO #FFCDD2
            **ISSUES:**
            - No session basket
            - No user context
            - Must reconstruct from contract
        end note

        FO -> DB: INSERT oxorder
        WH -> Contract: commitToOrder()

        ... later ...

        B -> RF: checkoutSuccess()
        RF -> Contract: Already COMMITTED
        RF --> B: Redirect to thankyou
    else Option B: Webhook Waits (Current)
        WH -> WH: Contract not ready
        WH --> Stripe: 200 OK\n(acknowledged, wait for user)

        note right of WH #E8F5E9
            **SAFE:**
            Let user flow complete order
            Webhook just confirms
        end note
    end
end

... later ...

Stripe --> B: Redirect to success_url
B -> RF: checkoutSuccess()
RF -> Contract: fulfillCondition()
RF -> FO: finalizeOrder()
FO --> RF: ORDER_STATE_OK

== Scenario 3: User Never Returns ==

note over C, DB #FFF3E0
    **EDGE CASE**
    User closes browser after payment
end note

C -> Stripe: Complete payment
C -> C: Close browser (never returns)

Stripe -> WH: payment_intent.succeeded
WH -> Contract: Find by provider_order_id
Contract --> WH: Contract (PENDING)

note right of WH
    **QUESTION:**
    How long do we wait?
    Payment is confirmed but no order.

    **Options:**
    1. Create order from webhook
    2. Keep payment without order
    3. Eventually refund
end note

== Proposed Solution ==

note over Contract, DB #C8E6C9
    **Contract-First Webhook Handling**

    1. Webhook ALWAYS acknowledges immediately (200 OK)
    2. Webhook updates contract with payment confirmation
    3. Contract tracks "payment_confirmed" flag
    4. User return flow checks flag and creates order
    5. If no return within timeout, background job:
       - Loads confirmed contracts without orders
       - Creates orders from contract data
       - Sends confirmation email
end note

@enduml
